\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Conceptually, the \gls {psl} will be made up of four components: the NRPO, two neoVAN-4S-HP amplifiers and the \gls {pmc} cavity. The \gls {npro} provides seed light with good noise characteristics. These noise characteristics are preserved by the amplifiers, so the resulting beam will have high power and low noise. As the linewidth of the \gls {pmc} $\sim \tmspace  -\thinmuskip {.1667em}1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\rm  {MHz}$, it filters away light in higher order modes and \gls {rf} intensity noise so a quiet spatially pure mode can be sent to the interferometer.\relax }}{34}{figure.caption.12}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapterconcept}{{2.1}{34}{Conceptually, the \gls {psl} will be made up of four components: the NRPO, two neoVAN-4S-HP amplifiers and the \gls {pmc} cavity. The \gls {npro} provides seed light with good noise characteristics. These noise characteristics are preserved by the amplifiers, so the resulting beam will have high power and low noise. As the linewidth of the \gls {pmc} $\sim \!1\,\rm {MHz}$, it filters away light in higher order modes and \gls {rf} intensity noise so a quiet spatially pure mode can be sent to the interferometer.\relax }{figure.caption.12}{}}
