\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.7}{\ignorespaces The top panel shows the power that was incident on the \gls {pmc} and the power emerging from the \gls {pmc} over a 55 hour trail run. The light produced by the amplifiers did not change significantly for the duration of this measurement, however the transmitted light through the \gls {pmc} dropped from 111\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\watt } to, at its lowest, 107\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\watt }. This is likely due to the environmental conditions in the lab changing. The bottom panel shows the humidity of the lab. Changes in the humidity, which can be caused by a temperature change, coincide with changes in the power emerging from the \gls {pmc}. This indicates that the alignment or mode matching of the laser and the \gls {pmc} may be dependent on temperature due to e.g.\nobreakspace  {}the thermal expansion of optical mounts.\relax }}{46}{figure.caption.18}}
\newlabel{fig:ligolaserchapterpowerplot}{{2.7}{46}{The top panel shows the power that was incident on the \gls {pmc} and the power emerging from the \gls {pmc} over a 55 hour trail run. The light produced by the amplifiers did not change significantly for the duration of this measurement, however the transmitted light through the \gls {pmc} dropped from 111\,\si {\watt } to, at its lowest, 107\,\si {\watt }. This is likely due to the environmental conditions in the lab changing. The bottom panel shows the humidity of the lab. Changes in the humidity, which can be caused by a temperature change, coincide with changes in the power emerging from the \gls {pmc}. This indicates that the alignment or mode matching of the laser and the \gls {pmc} may be dependent on temperature due to e.g.~the thermal expansion of optical mounts.\relax }{figure.caption.18}{}}
