\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Sketch of the \gls {lo} (green) and signal (pink) beam paths in relation to other parts of the interferometer (see Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:ligolayout} and Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:detector_chapter_LIGO_layout}). The \gls {lo} beam emerges from PR2. Some of this light is used to control the interferometer, so BHDBS1 is needed to split the light. BHDM1 directs the \gls {lo} onto BHDBS2. The signal beam emerges from the \gls {srm}. It passes through the OFI and is reflected by OM0. The signal combines with the \gls {lo} on BHDBS2. The layout of the optics in HAM6 is shown in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:bhdforligochapterlayout5f}.\relax }}{140}{figure.caption.60}}
