\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces The sensitivity curve for the A+ detectors expressed in units of $\si {\radian /\sqrt  {Hz}}$. At frequencies above 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz, the noise is flat ($3.4\times 10^{-5}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\radian /\sqrt  {\hertz }}$) as it is dominated by shot noise. At lower frequencies, the noise is increased relative to shot noise due to radiation pressure, coating thermal noise and other noise sources. At 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\hertz }, the noise is $8\times 10^{-5}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\radian /\sqrt  {\hertz }}$.\relax }}{144}{figure.caption.62}}
