\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on the amount of path length noise that is acceptable between the \gls {as} and \gls {lo} beams. The blue line shows the sensitivity curve in units of path length noise between the \gls {as} and \gls {lo} beams, and the orange line shows the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics which combine the \gls {lo} and signal beam. At 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics is $4.9\times 10^{-13}\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\si {\metre /\sqrt  {\hertz }}$.\relax }}{146}{figure.caption.63}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterhrtsrequirement}{{4.5}{146}{The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on the amount of path length noise that is acceptable between the \gls {as} and \gls {lo} beams. The blue line shows the sensitivity curve in units of path length noise between the \gls {as} and \gls {lo} beams, and the orange line shows the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics which combine the \gls {lo} and signal beam. At 5\,Hz, the longitudinal motion requirement for the optics is $4.9\times 10^{-13}\,\si {\metre /\sqrt {\hertz }}$.\relax }{figure.caption.63}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces A sketch of the \gls {lo} and signal beam paths. The \gls {lo} beam path is shown in blue, and the signal beam is shown in red. The dashed arrow indicates the direction that the recombining beam splitter, BHDBS2, may move in. If BHDBS2 moves in this way, the phase of the signal beam has increased while the phase of the \gls {lo} beam has decreased at the point where the signal and \gls {lo} beams combine. This means that the recombination beam splitter motion needs to be counted twice in calculations of the phase noise requirement.\relax }}{147}{figure.caption.64}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbhddoublecounted}{{4.6}{147}{A sketch of the \gls {lo} and signal beam paths. The \gls {lo} beam path is shown in blue, and the signal beam is shown in red. The dashed arrow indicates the direction that the recombining beam splitter, BHDBS2, may move in. If BHDBS2 moves in this way, the phase of the signal beam has increased while the phase of the \gls {lo} beam has decreased at the point where the signal and \gls {lo} beams combine. This means that the recombination beam splitter motion needs to be counted twice in calculations of the phase noise requirement.\relax }{figure.caption.64}{}}
