\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces (a) Sketch of a Mach-Zehnder interferometer. The interference at BS2 depends on the difference in the phase of the two beams after BS1. (b) Sketch of an interferometer (IFO) with a balanced homodyne detection scheme. The IFO could be, for instance, a Michelson interferometer. The IFO adds a phase modulation to the signal beam, and this results in an intensity modulation in the combined beams after BS2. In essence, (b) is similar to (a).\relax }}{215}{figure.caption.91}}
\newlabel{fig:mzchaptermzsketch}{{7.1}{215}{(a) Sketch of a Mach-Zehnder interferometer. The interference at BS2 depends on the difference in the phase of the two beams after BS1. (b) Sketch of an interferometer (IFO) with a balanced homodyne detection scheme. The IFO could be, for instance, a Michelson interferometer. The IFO adds a phase modulation to the signal beam, and this results in an intensity modulation in the combined beams after BS2. In essence, (b) is similar to (a).\relax }{figure.caption.91}{}}
