\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.9}{\ignorespaces Sketch of the in-vacuum Mach-Zehnder. Laser light entered the vacuum system and was steered by suspended optics into a Mach-Zehnder interferometer. The first beam splitter and the two corner mirrors were in identical suspensions. The suspensions are described in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:mz_chapter_in_vac_susp}. The beam splitter for recombining the beam was part of a larger suspended assembly which also included steering mirrors and the photodiodes. Photographs of the components are shown in Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:mzchapterinvacuummzapparatus}. The mirrors and the beam splitter were suspended with identical suspensions, and the recombining beam splitter was part of a larger assembly.\relax }}{229}{figure.caption.99}}
