\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B.7}{\ignorespaces The AD797 stage of the circuit (right) is a transimpedance amplifier for measuring the shot noise of 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}mA photocurrents. The left-hand stage of the circuit is used to provide the reverse bias for the photodiode. One input of this stage is a low-pass filter with two poles at 16\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz. A bench-top power supply would be connected to this input (V\_BIAS). The other input, (V\_MOD), was used to provide a modulation to the reverse bias voltage.\relax }}{265}{figure.caption.127}}
